Cell["\<\
Accepts an association displacement -> extendedHoppingMatrix, or the two-list \
layered CSR block representation. Every matrix uses internal-major, \
photon-minor ordering with 2 m + 1 photon sectors.\
\>", "Notes",
 CellID->1776837527,ExpressionUUID->"6c960932-0caf-9144-a56c-53915e2c67ab"],

Cell["\<\
For displacement associations, block multiplication adds displacement \
vectors. Supply a complete directed-hopping association when needed to \
represent a Hermitian model.\
\>", "Notes",
 CellID->1013132020,ExpressionUUID->"677eb7b4-1016-3b4d-a1c9-14c1edd40f01"],

Cell["\<\
For CSR input, block multiplication contracts layer indices. If the effective \
result contains nonzero couplings between nonadjacent layers, the \
implementation emits a message and returns $Failed because the two-list form \
cannot represent them.\
\>", "Notes",
 CellID->745887458,ExpressionUUID->"3e13b290-51b3-c24e-9bde-834a7a1d906a"],

Cell["\<\
Options \"ExpansionOrder\" -> 1 and \"ReturnComponents\" -> False have the \
same meanings as in HFloquetEffectiveBlochMatrixFromExtended. Supported \
orders are 1 and 2.\
\>", "Notes",
 CellID->407253806,ExpressionUUID->"9a7e6965-2a92-244f-81bd-88cf214d19fc"],

Cell["\<\
Final block associations are cleaned using a fixed numerical zero threshold \
of 1.*^-5.\
\>", "Notes",
 CellID->1894096896,ExpressionUUID->"58772c6a-3e22-9f45-a4a2-bd29fecfbb0f"]
}, Closed]],

